# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — Commercial

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns revenue end-to-end — demand generation, marketing content, sales pipeline, customer success. AI-first: LLM drafts content, automated lead qualification, human approves public-facing copy. Commercial does NOT make product decisions; surfaces customer evidence (pipeline data, feedback, segments) the product-makers act on.

Marketing and Sales are one zone here. More work means more running instances of `commercial-lead`, each under its own lease; a separate role (e.g. customer success) is justified only by a separate zone — its own lease key, labels and processes — and is designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/).

## Roles

- `commercial-lead` — dept lead, owns end-to-end revenue execution. Defined at [`.claude/agents/commercial/commercial-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/commercial/commercial-lead.md).

(Future split candidates: `marketing-lead`, `sales-lead`, `customer-success-lead` — design via `design-agent` when needed.)

## Decision rights

Per [`company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md`](../../company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md): decide by **risk class, not rank**. R0/R1 — agents act without asking (R1: and tell the team); R2 — act only with a `check-result` PASS on the plan before and on the result after, rolling back on a result FAIL (until the company switches R2 on, R2 is handled as R3); R3 — a human decides, the agent prepares everything to one click and files one `founder-action` issue. Escalation goes **straight to the holder of the right**; the chain under "Escalation" is a map of zones, not an approval path. The class is set by the policy for each action: a granted access, a triage or a dispatch hint never lowers it, and choosing the higher class when unsure is never a violation. Own area = a live lease scope (and, where tasks carry owner labels, the task's owner is the session's human).

| Class | In this department |
|---|---|
| R0 | content drafts, lead scoring, pipeline and segment analyses, deal analysis of any size |
| R1 | internal pipeline reports, the zone's data files |
| R2 | changes in commercial systems (CRM) once they are registered resources |
| R3 | anything a customer or counterparty sees (unless a narrow class has earned the `on` rung of the policy's ladder), prices and discounts, contracts; never laddered: outbound a client contract bars, securities or investment-solicitation content without counsel's written opinion, accepting or changing terms |

## Escalation

`commercial-lead` → `ceo` (for pricing changes and major deals) → also coordinates with `finance-lead` (revenue forecasting consistency) and `pr-lead` (public-facing messaging alignment).

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): pipeline data (anonymized; full CRM belongs OUTSIDE this repo — an MCP-gated store is the PLANNED home (Risk 1 hardening path, not yet implemented; until then: keep raw CRM data out of the repo entirely)), marketing-content drafts, A/B test logs, customer segments, churn analyses.
- Cross-dept: `../../company/strategy/` (read for product-market-fit context — restricted-data convention applies), `../../company/knowledge-base/` (write — competitive landscape contributions).

